<report>
<title>Fully nested/hierarchical random analysis of variance</title>

<p>Variables:<in>tlist</in></p>

<table>
<tr><th>Source of Variation</th><th>Sum Squares</th><th>DF</th><th>Mean Square</th></tr>
<tr><td>Between Groups</td><td><inu>grp_sum</inu></td><td><in>grp_df</in></td><td><inu>grp_mean</inu></td></tr>
<tr><td>Between Subgroups within Groups</td><td><inu>sub_sum</inu></td><td><in>sub_df</in></td><td><inu>sub_mean</inu></td></tr>
<tr><td>Residual</td><td><inu>res_sum</inu></td><td><in>res_df</in></td><td><inu>res_mean</inu></td></tr>
<tr><td>Total</td><td><inu>tot_sum</inu></td><td><in>tot_df</in></td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<p>F (VR between groups) = <inu>f_1</inu>  <pval><inp>p_1</inp></pval></p>

<p>F (using group/subgroup msqr) = <inu>f_2</inu>  <pval><inp>p_2</inp></pval></p>

<p>F (VR between subgroups within groups) = <inu>f_3</inu>  <pval><inp>p_3</inp></pval></p>
</report>
